00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:20.330
to find a place for the character

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:22.890
in an era of evolving
gender norms that mainstream

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.010
entertainment was expected to at least pay

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:27.640
lip service to. They
even use the question,

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:30.480
is there still a place in
the modern world for a secret

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.080
agent like 007 in promotional materials,

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:35.630
explicitly playing to the idea of Bond

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:38.040
as an anachronism rather
than hiding from it.

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:40.640
And while the Brosnan
Bond movies were still too

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:42.210
lighthearted to fully persuade

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:44.530
us of Bond's contemporary relevance,

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:46.640
the man who would inherit
his double O status

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:49.300
would be far better equipped. in a sense,

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:50.880
the broodier, bloodier direction,

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:53.770
which Daniel Craig took the
Bond franchise was really the

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:56.500
only place for it to go by 2006.

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:59.270
After years of full-blown
parodies like Austin Powers

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:00.590
and Johnny English took aim at

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:03.080
all the series tropes and cliches,

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:06.350
the goofy self-deprecating
humor of Brosnan and Moore

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:08.230
just wouldn't really work anymore.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.710
- What are you feeding him?

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:11.390
Why don't ya just kill'em?

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:14.350
- No, Scott, I have an even better idea.

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:17.230
I'm going to place them in
an easily escapable situation

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:20.010
involving an overly
elaborate and exotic death.

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:21.560
- [Michael] So you couldn't really expect

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:24.870
an audience to sit through that
style of a bond movie again,

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.000
with a straight face.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:27.110
And at the same time,

00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:29.730
the success of the Bourne
movies had ushered in an era of

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:32.140
more serious, grounded spy thrillers.

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:34.950
James Bond couldn't just be a
well-groomed jokester anymore.

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:37.620
He had to be convincing as
a trained killer and more

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:40.510
fundamentally as an actual human being.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:42.910
We needed a Bond who could
do the heavier lifting

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:45.980
dramatically speaking that was
expected of a spy thriller in

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:47.410
the 21st century.

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:49.480
Enter Daniel Craig.

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:52.150
When Craig emerges from the
water glistening under the sun

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:54.400
and showing off his bulked up body,

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:56.620
it's not just for the eye candy.

00:11:56.620 --> 00:12:00.070
It's making us viscerally
aware of Bond's body so that we

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:02.623
can watch the toll his
work is going to take.

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:05.440
The Craig Bond films highlight the

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:07.310
battering that he takes
throughout each mission,

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:10.430
showing his injuries and
all their grisly detail and

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:12.780
emphasizing the gruesome
things he has to put himself

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:14.973
through just to stay alive.

00:12:14.973 --> 00:12:18.563
(Dramatic Music sting)

00:12:18.563 --> 00:12:19.396
(Bond groans painfully)

00:12:19.396 --> 00:12:21.430
Bond still made plenty of
time for games of chance

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:23.010
and romantic dalliances.

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:26.440
But the true stakes of his
behavior are always made clear.

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:29.990
He lives a life of constant
danger, not freewheeling fun.

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:33.170
And it's more devil may care
decisions often come with

00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:34.890
devastating consequences.

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:36.660
- Look how well your charm works James.

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:38.530
- [Michael] The protagonist
might still be handsome

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:39.470
and quick with the line.

00:12:39.470 --> 00:12:41.080
- Can you kill him?

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:41.913
- Yes.

00:12:43.554 --> 00:12:45.250
- Will you?

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:46.620
- Someone usually dies.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:49.470
- But he was someone whose
whole life revolves around doing

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:52.800
ugly, often morally questionable things.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:54.850
And this fact was reflected in the haunted

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:56.970
hard drinking new
version of the character.

00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:58.020
- Vodka Martini.

00:12:58.020 --> 00:12:59.020
- Shaken or stirred?

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:00.350
- Do I look like a give a damn?

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:02.090
- [Michael] As much as
he tries to maintain

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:04.680
the character's signature steely exterior.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.790
This is the first bond we see carrying

00:13:06.790 --> 00:13:09.156
his emotional wounds from film to film.

00:13:09.156 --> 00:13:10.790
- Well, he'd have to be
a pretty cold bastard

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:11.650
if you didn't want revenge

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:13.690
for the death of someone he loved.

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:16.210
- You don't have to worry about me.

00:13:16.210 --> 00:13:18.433
I'm not going to go chasing
him. He's not important.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:22.273
And Neither was she.

00:13:22.273 --> 00:13:24.130
- [Michael] In every other iteration,

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:27.320
007 seemed to reset
completely between missions.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:29.280
The agent turning up as crisp and clean

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:30.520
as his new dinner suit.

00:13:30.520 --> 00:13:32.661
By the time Craig's
version gets to Skyfall.

00:13:32.661 --> 00:13:36.840
The psychological and physical
toll of being James Bond is

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:38.310
made painfully clear.

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:42.840
- Medical evaluation: fail.
Physical evaluation: fail.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:44.760
Psychological evaluation:

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:48.220
alcohol and substance
addiction indicated, Ooh.

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:50.310
- [Michael] This moody brooding Bond

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:51.760
was not one designed for

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:55.309
nationalistic mythmaking,
but for a post 9/11 world,

00:13:55.309 --> 00:13:58.710
in which the brutality and
ambiguity of global conflicts was

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:02.340
being broadcasted daily.
It's a revisionist portrayal,

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:04.766
which owns the physical
and psychological damage,

00:14:04.766 --> 00:14:07.500
which our real life
James Bond would undergo.

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:09.720
It still gave audiences, the debonair,

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:12.360
all action fantasy that come to expect,

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:14.030
but it also complicated it.

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:17.210
Forcing them to reckon with
his coldness and his brutality.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:18.780
So at the end of the day,

00:14:18.780 --> 00:14:21.940
Bond has not only survived
explosions, bullet wounds,

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:23.270
and a razor rim tats,

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:25.930
but he's withstood the passage
of time more successfully

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:28.370
than almost any other pop culture figure.

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:30.790
So we're left with the
same question that everyone

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:33.640
from Dr. No to Blofeld has agonized over.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:36.490
Why is James Bond so damn hard to kill?

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:38.070
The answer might lie in the fact that

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:39.960
as an international man of mystery,

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:43.080
the question of who 007, exactly is,

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:46.210
is always been intentionally
shrouded in uncertainty.

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:49.130
Scholar, Christopher Lindner
suggests that the key to Bond's

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:52.750
longevity is his status as
a highly unstable and often

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:54.410
ambiguous cultural icon.

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:55.430
From his inception,

00:14:55.430 --> 00:14:58.410
Bond has always been less of
a flesh and blood man than a

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.740
kind of ideal.

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:01.700
His height, hair color, accent,

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:04.830
and general character have
all changed massively over the

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:07.990
years as he has gone from blowing
up bad guys with explosive

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:08.823
toothpaste.

00:15:08.823 --> 00:15:11.693
- Denternite Toothpaste:
to be used sparingly.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:14.700
it's the latest in plastic explosive.

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:17.570
- [Michael] To battling the
gruesome effects of age and

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:21.350
alcoholism and author Craig
Owens argues that, Bond is not

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:23.950
the collection of various
characteristics. Rather,

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:27.340
he is the blank middle they
fill in. He is an opening,

00:15:27.340 --> 00:15:29.980
a vacant, unclaimed potentiality,

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:33.070
rather than an ontologically
assignable identity.

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:36.150
And so, we get to fill Bonds' feign tuxedo

00:15:36.150 --> 00:15:37.660
with whoever we need him to be

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:39.410
at that moment in history,

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:42.510
his adventures have adapted
to our changing tastes

00:15:42.510 --> 00:15:45.550
with the campy gadget filled
iterations of the nineties,

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:46.930
giving way to the grittier

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:49.040
more grounded style of the 2000's.

00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:51.423
- Were you expecting an exploding pen?

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:54.950
We don't really go in for that anymore.

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:55.820
- As a result,

00:15:55.820 --> 00:15:59.080
Bond is able to retain his
appeal from one decade to the

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:02.430
next, even as tastes and
trends change completely.

00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:04.840
With a new incarnation of
the character arriving,

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:07.600
tailor made to meet
each audiences demands.

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:09.140
But what do you guys think?

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:11.450
Will there eventually come
a day where James Bond

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:13.710
simply has to be put into retirement?

00:16:13.710 --> 00:16:16.870
Or, is he such a potent
and plyable symbol,

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.990
that we can keep reinventing him forever?

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.410
Let us know in the comments.

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:23.000
Thanks, as always, to our
patrons for all your support.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.240
And remember to check out our podcast.

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:28.070
Wrestle that subscribe button,
like it's a pre CGI shark,

00:16:28.070 --> 00:16:30.000
and don't forget to ring that bell.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.491
And as always, thanks for watching, later.

00:16:32.491 --> 00:16:35.491
